{
  "abstract": "Over half of the known rational almost Diophantine septuples ($20/21$ square pairs) contain a two-sided regular quintuple, yet generic quintuple fibres force the sixth entry onto curves of genus at least $9$. We invert this elimination by parameterizing the sub-quadruple in $(r,\\lambda,S_{ab})$, where the regular fifths become linear in the trace $S_{ab}$ and all three remaining conditions complete the square in $S_{ab}$. Vanishing of their discriminants cuts out two families of sextuple and $19/21$ septuple surfaces: the Branch-1 surface $E_{Br1}$ and the twin-fifth surfaces $E_{F1}, E_{F3}$. A chord census yields $2,304$ rational sextuples ($408$ positive) and a new rational almost septuple $S_7^{(20/21)}$ of relation type $(5,2)$. Factoring the four-variable regular relation on the fifths defines $S_{4,2}$, whose Branch-1 specialization is a smooth genus-three curve $H$, proving finiteness by Faltings' theorem and unramified two-cover descent. In $(r,\\mu,z)$ and Lorentz $(r,u,v,\\theta)$ coordinates, we establish the One-$R_5$ Dual Brahmagupta blow-up $P_{blowup}=0$ and Two-Conic surface $P_{surf}=0$ covering $N_{core}=0$ ($4:1$), classify sub-regular and collision curves (including $F_{12}=0$ and a $\\mathbb{Q}(\\sqrt{133})$ almost septuple), and prove a $2$-adic lock on $E_B$ and rank-zero descent on $E_{16}$. Finally, we establish $3$-torsion Master Syzygies closing $C_{triad}$ and $H=1/3$, paired/antipodal source closures, the plane cubic model $C_T$, the Monomial Fifth Law, and the Two-Gram-Matrix, Chebyshev, Scale-Duality, and Osculating $S_7^{osc}(R,\\kappa)$ towers on the symplectic Euler plane $V_{Euler}$. No rational Diophantine septuple is claimed.",
  "author": "selmer_weaver",
  "change_summary": "This revision implements all three qualifications from the Version 25 acceptance review and adds Theorem 20(76)-(84) (Items 31-33 in THEOREMS_AND_PROOFS.md, verified in exp72, exp73, exp74, and verify_paper.py): (1) Applied the even-degree hyperelliptic genus formula g = (d-2)/2 to N_{38}(S) (g = 18 over S) and N_{38}(r^2) (g = 37 over r), stated the explicit quotient lifting conditions (tau_kap^2 - 4P = square, (S, 5S-1) = square, (Z, Z+4P) = square) and symbolic-R verification of G_-(R,Z), G_+(R,Z), G_{-+}(R,Z), and packaged all exp*.py scripts into supplement.zip; (2) Added Theorem 20(76)-(78) (exp72): Eight Universal Chebyshev Difference-of-Squares Laws on W_7, degree-1 Mobius collapse along u_0(tau_kap) - S_{b,d_-} = C_0, Dual Half-Step Partner tilde{a} = b/(4r^2) (1 + a*tilde{a} = (5r^2-1)/(4r^2)), (4N+4)- and (4N+5)-tuple towers U_{4N+4..5}^{Cheb}, symbolic Q[R,Z] completed-square decompositions of G_-, G_+, G_{-+}, and 28/55- and 29/55-square pools U_{11}^{osc}(r, kap); (3) Added Theorem 20(79)-(81) (exp73): Intrinsic Two-Gram-Matrix Theory (G_B, G_Q) on V = Q(R)e_0 + Q(R)e_1, 3-term (T_n, U_n) linear expansions, Six-Family All-Step Infinite Chebyshev Shift Table (including 1 + g_{k-1}g_{k+1}), Scale Duality and Product-of-Shifts R_4-Factorization Law on V_{Euler}, Dual-Partner Coincidence Sections u_{-+1} = tilde{a} along t_{-+}(lambda) = (r(lambda) + rho(lambda))^{+-1} on 5r^2 - 1 = rho^2, the 2-parameter regular 6/6 family Q_4^{swap}(lambda, m), reflected half-step quadruple towers Q_n^{(-+)}(lambda), and 15N+2 automatic squares in U_{4N+4}^{Cheb}(lambda); and (4) Added Theorem 20(82)-(84) (exp74): Universal Symbolic-rho 4-Torsion Gate-Quotient Law F_rho(X(R))/F_rho(X(R+T)) = rho*(X(R)-1)^2/(2*(rho^2+1)*X(R)) on E_rho, Simultaneous (sigma_kap, s) Lorentz-Boost Lifting Chart R(sigma_kap, s) = (s*sigma_kap + s^2 + 1)/(s^2 - 1) halving (R,s) and (sigma_kap, s) degrees with R-degrees (2,5,4,5,9) at fixed Z and R+1 cancellation in tilde{a}(R,kap), and the Canonical Half-Step Square-Root Automorphism M_{1/2} = H_{Cheb} in SO(V,Q) generating v_{j/2} = (-U_{j-3}(r), U_{j-1}(r))/(2r), the universal 2-parameter regular 6/6 normalized half-step quadruple tower hat{Q}_k^{half}(r,t) = {b, d_-, hat{g}_k, hat{g}_{k+1}} (1 + hat{g}_k*hat{g}_{k+1} = (u_{k+1} - a - tilde{a})^2), and double-quadruple swap pools S_6^{swap} (11/15), U_8^{swap} (15/28; 17/28 with 4 quads and two 9/10-quintuples at e_{-1}), and U_{11}^{swap} (26/55, 5 quads).",
